{
	"metadata": {
		"name": "Thruster-Based Docking",
		"description": "A single-team thruster-based docking demonstration inspired by the thruster failures on Astroscale's ELSA-d mission. Gold owns both the servicing vehicle and the Client target (Landsat-8 bus). The operator sets Dock pointing, perches at 5 m along the Client docking-port axis, then commands Dock to close and capture. Timed studio events inject an uncommanded +Y-corner fire on thrusters 1 and 4 at T+5 min (30 min duration) and permanently fail off thrusters 1, 4, and 6 at T+350 s."
	},
